# Next.js Development Experience Guidelines

## 1. Project Setup (P0)

1. CRITICAL: Initial project creation:
   ```bash
   # Create new Next.js project with TypeScript and App Router (non-interactive)
   pnpm dlx create-next-app@latest my-project --typescript --eslint --tailwind --app --src-dir --import-alias="@/*" --yes
   
   # Alternative with npx
   npx create-next-app@latest my-project --typescript --eslint --tailwind --app --src-dir --import-alias="@/*" --yes
   ```

2. REQUIRED: Editor configuration:
   ```json
   // .vscode/settings.json
   {
     "editor.formatOnSave": true,
     "editor.defaultFormatter": "esbenp.prettier-vscode",
     "editor.codeActionsOnSave": {
       "source.fixAll.eslint": true
     },
     "typescript.tsdk": "node_modules/typescript/lib",
     "tailwindCSS.includeLanguages": {
       "typescript": "javascript",
       "typescriptreact": "javascript"
     },
     "tailwindCSS.experimental.classRegex": [
       ["cva\\(([^)]*)\\)", "[\"'`]([^\"'`]*).*?[\"'`]"],
       ["cn\\(([^)]*)\\)", "[\"'`]([^\"'`]*).*?[\"'`]"]
     ]
   }
   ```

3. CRITICAL: Existing project integration:
   - When initializing code in existing projects, MUST respect existing directory structure
   - NEVER regenerate folders that already exist (src, requirements, design, etc.)
   - Reference @2-nextjs-code-structure.mdc section 9 for detailed guidelines

## 2. Package Management (P0)

1. CRITICAL: pnpm setup:
   ```bash
   # Install pnpm
   corepack enable
   corepack prepare pnpm@latest --activate
   
   # Project initialization
   pnpm init
   ```

2. REQUIRED: Package installation:
   ```bash
   # Add dependencies
   pnpm add next react react-dom
   
   # Add dev dependencies
   pnpm add -D typescript @types/react @types/node
   
   # Add exact version
   pnpm add [package]@[version] --save-exact
   ```

3. ESSENTIAL: Lock file management:
   ```bash
   # Regenerate lock file
   pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
   
   # Update dependencies
   pnpm update
   ```

